WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.034
In keeping with his

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:01.801
reality TV

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.502
roots, the former

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.636
president preempted

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.005
any Justice Department

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.406
announcement of the charges

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.441
against him in a series of post

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.110
on his social media network.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.845
And one, just a few moments ago,

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:12.879
he wrote, quote,

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.447
I have been summoned to appear

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:15.615
at the federal courthouse

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:18.251
in Miami on Tuesday at 3 p.m..

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:19.452
He goes on to say,

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:20.787
he never thought it was possible

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.822
that such a thing like this could happen.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:23.456
Then drifts

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.491
into boasting about

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.692
how he won all the votes

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.093
in the presidential election,

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.561
which we know is not true.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.630
He also wrote in all caps, quote,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.165
I am an innocent man.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:32.999
Kaitlin joining us now,

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.501
our senior Justice Department

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.036
correspondent, Evan Perez.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:36.736
Evan,

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.272
what do we know about these seven counts

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.874
Well, we don't know the details

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.575
of exactly what these seven counts are.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.043
Anderson,

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.078
we know that the former president

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.046
was on notice.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.947
He knew that he was being investigated

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.183
for a couple of particular statutes.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.252
One is seven 93, the Espionage Act.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.054
That's the willful retention

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.622
of national defense information.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.090
We know he was also notified

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.460
that he was under investigation for 2071,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.061
which is

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.062
a concealment

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.297
of these documents, government documents,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.099
depriving them

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:06.766
from the use

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.301
of federal government officials

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.869
and, of course, obstruction of justice.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.938
The question is what other charges,

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:12.772
possible charges?

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.774
We know that there are seven charges.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.643
And, you know, again,

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:17.744
the fact is that

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.145
this has never happened before.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.247
And this is something that,

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:21.481
you know,

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.148
the Jack Smith,

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.517
the prosecutors in that office

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.854
have weighed for some time before

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:28.955
making this decision.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.256
Everything, including,

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:30.690
of course,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.591
the target letter

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.893
that the former president received

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.895
only recently

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.298
had to go through Merrick Garland,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.999
Merrick Garland, the attorney general

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.801
would have had to review this and decide

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.803
whether to to allow it to go forward.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:47.607
So the idea that this this indictment

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:48.007
we don't know

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.175
exactly when it was returned,

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:49.876
if it was returned

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.044
today, he's certainly

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.112
the former president says

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.980
he was notified this evening.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.115
It tells us that,

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:55.381
you know,

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.483
the Justice Department

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.618
had certainly gotten to this stage

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.488
very recently, that they knew

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.555
they had enough evidence,

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.457
they believe they had enough evidence

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.059
to bring this to a jury.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.827
And also just talk about

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.429
this being in Florida,

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.064
the change of venue.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.165
Yeah, no, actually,

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:12.565
Anderson,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.800
this is one of the fascinating things

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.400
for us.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.435
We've been following this.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.470
We've seen dozens of witnesses

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.005
go to the federal courthouse

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.240
here in Washington

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.841
and and be brought

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.877
before the grand jury here

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.612
that was hearing witnesses

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:26.546
again, testimony

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.881
with regard to this

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.883
and the January six investigation.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.784
And it's only recently that we understand

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.920
that this grand jury in Miami

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.055
started hearing testimony.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.991
What we heard from Trump lawyers,

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.292
including on our air,

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.393
was that they believe

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.561
there was an issue with venue.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.162
We're told that

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:42.729
this is something

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.830
they raised

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.398
with the Justice Department,

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.533
that they believed

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.700
it would be improper

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.269
to bring this case in Washington

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:51.337
because any possible crimes,

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.972
any accusations against the former

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.240
president happened

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.975
in the Southern District of Florida.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:58.311
Which is, of course, where Mar a Lago is

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.679
is located.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.781
It appears, Anderson, that Justice

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:02.882
Department officials

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.384
eventually got to that point.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.452
They clearly were at some point

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.420
thought it would be better

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.721
to do it here in Washington,

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.256
but then changed their mind

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:10.990
and decided

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.692
that Miami is the place

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.660
to bring these charges.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.761
Again, we don't know

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.396
the exact details of these charges.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:17.664
But clearly,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.064
you know,

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:21.100
that's why this sudden change of venue

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.503
and now we expect the former president

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.772
to appear on Tuesday

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.940
for his first appearance

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.541
before a magistrate in Miami.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.243
Yeah, he said 3 p.m..

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.477
Evan, we'll check back in

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:32.712
with you, though, over the next 2 hours.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:33.112
I'm joined now

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.480
by our political and legal analyst,

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:34.981
New York Times.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.382
Maggie, Haberman, former Obama senior

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.951
adviser David Axelrod, former

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:38.618
assistant U.S.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:39.152
Attorney Ali

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.486
Hoenig, and Republican strategist

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:41.721
David Urban, one time campaign

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.389
adviser to the former president.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.991
Maggie, I want to start with you.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.726
What are you hearing, first of all?

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:47.193
Well,

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.095
I think everyone is still in shock

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:49.762
is hearing the news,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.631
both people around the former president

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.398
and frankly, people

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.433
across the political spectrum,

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.300
because we have been hearing

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.536
the drip, drip of this case for so long.

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:57.670
His team was prepared

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.404
for this to happen

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.038
this week,

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.073
didn't have information

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.507
that it was going to.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.209
Seven counts is a lot.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:03.509
You know,

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.377
we don't know exactly

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.478
what all of the charges are yet.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:06.246
We're going to have to see

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.080
what the complaint is.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.580
We won't know

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.916
until presumably it's unsealed.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:11.217
So there's a lot of unknowns.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.452
But this is obviously not

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.486
a good development.

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:13.886
And it's one

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.155
that he was hoping to avoid listening.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.624
From a legal perspective,

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.692
what do you think the seven counts are?

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.194
So what do we what do we know

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.929
based on what's been presented thus far?

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:23.963
The best indicator

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:24.697
we have so far

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.232
is the search warrant affidavit

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:27.033
from Mar a Lago.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.301
And when the Justice Department

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:28.968
went to a judge,

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.104
they said we have probable cause

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:31.571
to believe

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:32.672
that three different crimes

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.306
were committed,

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:34.374
willful retention

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.576
or mishandling of defense information.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.043
That's part

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.611
of the Espionage Act

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.312
destruction

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.281
or concealment of government documents.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:43.449
And then third, obstruction of justice.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.917
Now, federal prosecutors

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.753
can break this out any way they want.

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:47.420
It's possible

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.689
we see multiple counts of some of those.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:50.456
It's possible

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:51.124
we see

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.525
any combination of those

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.526
that adds up to seven

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.595
it could be that we see other accounts

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:56.763
because what

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.630
you put in your search warrant

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.132
affidavit may not necessarily be

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.733
what you indict on an Anderson.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:01.868
Bigger picture,

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.603
even without seeing the specifics

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.937
of this indictment.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:05.605
I think it's clear

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.639
that Donald Trump is in

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.041
for the fight of his life.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:12.045
This is a man who has been sued, deposed,

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.480
taken the fifth impeached, twice

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.582
tried in the Senate,

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.718
investigated by Congress, even indicted

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:19.752
by the state

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:20.720
authorities here in Manhattan,

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.255
but being indicted by the Justice

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:23.556
Department is different.

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.158
This is a whole different ballgame.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.093
DOJ has way more resources.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.928
The conduct here is going to be,

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.029
I think it's safe to say,

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:30.930
more significant

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.332
than what he was indicted for

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:33.032
in Manhattan.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:33.900
The consequences

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:34.567
if he's convicted

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.135
are going to be much more severe

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.537
than what he's looking at in Manhattan.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.739
What about there was an espionage

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:41.641
charge as a possibility?

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.141
Yeah, that

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.943
that is one of the crimes that was listed

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:46.112
and that relates to mishandling

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.180
of defense information,

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.115
not necessarily classified information.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.717
I should note this also,

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:51.918
one of the statutes

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.653
that was listed in the search warrant

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:55.221
application destruction

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:56.889
and concealment of government documents

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.324
says on the face of the law,

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:00.393
if a person is convicted of this crime,

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.961
he's disqualified

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:03.129
from holding federal office.

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.130
Now, big thing

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.465
we need to know here,

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.266
that may not be constitutional.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.968
That's never been challenged in court.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:09.936
I think there's a good chance

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:11.037
that that would not hold up in court.

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:13.439
Also, I think it's unlikely.

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.507
What we don't know

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:16.342
whether this case will be tried

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:17.043
before the election.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.211
And even if it is,

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.112
nothing is final

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.213
until the appeal is over,

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.214
that will not happen.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:22.648
Until after the election.

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:23.216
David.

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:23.750
David Irving,

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.218
I mean, you know,

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:26.886
the former president quite well.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:29.088
His statement on his social media,

00:06:29.756 --> 00:06:30.723
it paints a picture

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:32.525
of how he's going to portray this,

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:33.059
obviously.

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.560
But it's you know,

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.662
we saw this kind of played out in an ad

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:38.030
that the wolves are coming for me.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:40.099
Right, that the campaign has put together

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:41.134
and we've heard this,

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:41.834
you know, over and over that

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.103
I'm standing between you and them. Right.

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:45.071
That the Justice Department

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:47.039
had weaponized FBI and weaponized.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:47.807
You know,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:48.541
one of the points

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.343
I think makes it tougher here

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:53.012
is this Espionage Act charge right now.

00:06:53.279 --> 00:06:54.013
And we don't know

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:54.847
if that's one of the seven.

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:55.948
Well, I don't know what the seven counts,

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:58.017
but based upon the search warrant, it's,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.685
you know, the Espionage Act

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:00.787
when you paint yourself

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:01.921
and you and you're a patriot

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:02.488
and you

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:03.156
you're the president

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:03.890
of the United States,

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:07.860
I can't imagine a worse phrase to be used

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:09.395
with the president, United States

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.731
than the espionage act, when you hear it.

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:12.498
It just it

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.801
it makes you sick to your stomach. Right.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:15.902
And so I think people

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.537
